network-manager-zerotier (0.2.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add nm-zerotier-reconciled, a persistent systemd service that
    continuously reconciles NetworkManager's view of ZeroTier VPN
    connections against zerotier-one's actual joined-network state in
    both directions: activates the matching NM connection when a network
    is joined externally (e.g. via zerotier-cli or another tool), and
    deactivates it when left externally. Networks joined externally with
    no matching NM connection profile at all are imported automatically
    once their tun interface exists, same as
    contrib/import-zerotier-networks.sh.
  * Remove the previous one-directional, per-connection 15s drift monitor
    from nm-zerotier-plugin.c; nm-zerotier-reconciled is now the single
    source of truth for ongoing reconciliation.
  * New build dependency: systemd-dev (for the systemd unit install
    directory).

 -- Ivo Lucas <ivolucas@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 15:41:56 +0100

network-manager-zerotier (0.1.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Expand the editor's read-only "ZeroTier status" section with name,
    type, MAC, MTU, pushed routes, and the network's permission/feature
    flags (managed/global/default-route/DNS, bridge/broadcast), fetched
    from zerotier-cli's full JSON output instead of just status and
    assigned addresses.
  * Add a refresh button next to the status section so it can be
    re-queried (against whatever network id is currently typed) without
    closing and reopening the connection editor.

 -- Ivo Lucas <ivolucas@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:24:53 +0100

network-manager-zerotier (0.1.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add post-connect monitoring: if a ZeroTier network is left outside
    NetworkManager (e.g. via zerotier-cli or another tool) while the VPN
    connection is active, the connection is now reported as failed
    instead of NetworkManager showing a stale "connected" state.
  * Add contrib/import-zerotier-networks.sh to create NetworkManager VPN
    connections for ZeroTier networks already joined outside NM.

 -- Ivo Lucas <ivolucas@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 13:49:22 +0100

